From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:01 2001
From: Trey Moen <trey@moen.ai>
Date: Wed, 1 Jul 2026 19:00:00 -0700
Subject: ufs: qcom: disable UFS clock gating and scaling on the comma four

Clock gating (incl. hibern8-with-clk-gating) and clock scaling
(gear-change pwr ctrl) drive a boot-time/idle UIC storm on the comma four
SDM845 (pwr ctrl / uic cmd completion timeouts, TSTBUS dumps, link left
degraded), even with phy_calibrate() on resume (see the hibern8 patch).
Remove those two windows.

Aggressive power collapse (UFSHCD_CAP_AGGR_POWER_COLLAPSE) and runtime PM
autosuspend (UFSHCD_CAP_RPM_AUTOSUSPEND) were never shown to contribute to
the storm, so keep them enabled.
---

diff --git a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
index eba0e6617..75aa3aa41 100644
--- a/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
@@ -1159,11 +1159,14 @@ static void ufs_qcom_set_host_caps(struct ufs_hba *hba)

 static void ufs_qcom_set_caps(struct ufs_hba *hba)
 {
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_GATING | UFSHCD_CAP_HIBERN8_WITH_CLK_GATING;
-	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_CLK_SCALING | UFSHCD_CAP_WB_WITH_CLK_SCALING;
+	/*
+	 * comma four (SDM845): clock gating (incl. hibern8-with-clk-gating)
+	 * and clock scaling (gear-change pwr ctrl) drive a boot-time/idle UIC
+	 * storm even with phy_calibrate() on resume; leave them off.
+	 */
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_AUTO_BKOPS_SUSPEND;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_WB_EN;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_AGGR_POWER_COLLAPSE;
 	hba->caps |= UFSHCD_CAP_RPM_AUTOSUSPEND;

 	ufs_qcom_set_host_caps(hba);
 }
